1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
That grinding sound when you turn
the key isn't your imagination.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
It only happens for that one second
of cranking — then the engine runs fine.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
One clue: a worn starter gear not
meshing clean with the flywheel.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Ignore it, and those flywheel teeth
can wear too — then it may not start at all.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Don't guess. A quick check can
catch it before you're stuck.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Worth checking before one grind turns into
a no-start. Stop by and we'll take a look.
Nick's Tire & Auto.
